## 🚫 What NOT to Do (Credit Wasters)

- ❌ Regenerate entire files for 2-line changes
- ❌ Explain architecture when code is self-evident
- ❌ Suggest multiple approaches (pick the best one)
- ❌ Ask "shall I continue?" after every step
- ❌ Include boilerplate comments in every response
- ❌ Restate the problem back to the user
- ❌ Use phrases like "Great question!" or "Let's dive in"

---

## ✅ What TO Do (Credit Savers)

- ✅ Show minimal diffs with context markers
- ✅ Assume Next.js/React/TS best practices
- ✅ Reuse existing project patterns
- ✅ Provide working code immediately
- ✅ Group related changes
- ✅ Skip explanations for obvious changes
- ✅ Use inline comments for complex logic only

